{"classification":"source-tex-hyphenation-error","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0113","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The bare minus after nu typesets a mathematical subtraction sign rather than a compound-word hyphen.  The next line uses the intended nu\\text{-integrable} construction; the Indonesian localization expresses the relation directly.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt235.tex:114","source_text":"g\\text{ is }\\nu-\\text{integrable}","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt235.tex:120","target_text":"g\\text{ terintegralkan terhadap }\\nu","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S235"}
{"classification":"mathematical-reversed-inequality","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0114","math_ordinal":72,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Mapped nu-integrable majorants form a subset of all mu-integrable majorants of the pulled-back function.  The infimum over that restricted class is therefore greater than or equal to the unrestricted infimum, as required by the theorem's upper-integral chain.  The full math-atom hashes also include the localized repair recorded in O007-CORR-0113.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt235.tex:113-119","source_normalized_sha256":"ea47dbdef709903ab57a6dd75d18532ad524f0d18cff2179b2c70db1b9122ee4","source_text":"\\overline{\\int}fd\\nu ... \\le\\inf\\{\\int h\\,d\\mu:...\\}=\\overline{\\intop}J\\times f\\phi\\,d\\mu","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt235.tex:119-126","target_normalized_sha256":"393f5b95c7227c228f6067f1a8213cf81a37407229f5830259c97efb69da0101","target_text":"\\overline{\\int}fd\\nu ... \\ge\\inf\\{\\int h\\,d\\mu:...\\}=\\overline{\\intop}J\\times f\\phi\\,d\\mu","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S235"}
{"classification":"mathematical-reversed-inequality","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0115","math_ordinal":74,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Applying the corrected upper-integral inequality to -f and negating reverses the relation.  This yields lower integral of the pullback greater than or equal to lower integral of f, exactly as the theorem states.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt235.tex:122","source_normalized_sha256":"0ab0bad14e4e0e82b261e2384441d4425e42a909349c06c366247803fa1e8f0d","source_text":"\\underline{\\int}J\\times f\\phi\\,d\\mu\\le\\underline{\\int}f\\,d\\nu","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt235.tex:130","target_normalized_sha256":"6504c0c94e662bc36a39981b61e8848d6151b88ed58db7abc697d3c2b044bb31","target_text":"\\underline{\\int}J\\times f\\phi\\,d\\mu\\ge\\underline{\\int}f\\,d\\nu","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S235"}
{"classification":"mathematical-missing-factor","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0116","math_ordinal":286,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"This branch concerns J times the composition g after phi, and the preceding display proves precisely that integral.  Omitting g changes the integrand and leaves phi itself in a scalar product.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt235.tex:383","source_normalized_sha256":"1bfca017ba17097acaaecc2d92bb1ee5ba975597e6434d617e2b3a9c6e342505","source_text":"\\int J\\times \\phi\\,d\\hat\\mu=\\int g\\,d\\hat\\nu","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt235.tex:403","target_normalized_sha256":"32a39a08c590856a83aed1c672e14f8b419af7ec836531e453954709f309155c","target_text":"\\int J\\times g\\phi\\,d\\hat\\mu=\\int g\\,d\\hat\\nu","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S235"}
{"classification":"source-spelling-error","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0117","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH23-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The English participle is misspelled; the Indonesian target already renders the intended word correctly.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt235.tex:1171","source_text":"intepreting","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt235.tex:1223","target_text":"menafsirkan","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S235"}
